# Development Workflow - Agent Requested

This rule provides comprehensive setup and workflow commands for the LangGraph RAG project.

> **📋 Configuration Reference**: See @project-fundamentals for all service URLs, model names, and configuration constants.

## Environment Setup Commands

### Initial Setup
```bash
# Install dependencies using uv
uv sync

# Start Docker services (Ollama and Qdrant)
docker-compose up -d

# Verify Docker services
docker-compose ps

# Check services are healthy (URLs from project-fundamentals)
curl http://localhost:11434/api/tags  # Ollama - from project-fundamentals
curl http://localhost:6333/collections  # Qdrant - from project-fundamentals
```

### Ollama Model Management
```bash
# Check Ollama version (should be 0.11.10+)
ollama -v

# Pull required models (names from project-fundamentals)
ollama pull gpt-oss:20b  # From project-fundamentals
ollama pull embeddinggemma:latest  # From project-fundamentals

# List available models
ollama list

# Test model (optional, model name from project-fundamentals)
ollama run gpt-oss:20b "Hello, test message"  # From project-fundamentals
```

### Service URLs
> **Note**: All URLs defined in @project-fundamentals
- **Ollama API**: http://localhost:11434
- **Qdrant Dashboard**: http://localhost:6333/dashboard
- **Qdrant API**: http://localhost:6333

## Notebook Execution Order

### Workflow Steps
1. **First**: Run `Ollama_Setup_and_Testing.ipynb`
   - Verify Ollama installation and models
   - Test embeddings with LangChain connectors
   - Test model inference
   - Confirm all setup is working

2. **Second**: Run `Assignment_Introduction_to_LCEL_and_LangGraph_LangChain_Powered_RAG.ipynb`
   - Main assignment notebook
   - Implements the RAG system
   - Contains breakout room activities

3. **Kernel Selection**: Always select the venv created by `uv sync`

## Development Commands

### Service Management
```bash
# Start services in background
docker-compose up -d

# View service logs
docker-compose logs ollama
docker-compose logs qdrant

# Stop services
docker-compose down

# Restart services
docker-compose restart

# Check service status
docker-compose ps
```

### Python Environment
```bash
# Activate virtual environment (if needed)
source .venv/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac
# or
.venv\Scripts\activate  # Windows

# Run Python script
python lcel-langchain-langgraph.py

# Start Jupyter with correct kernel
jupyter notebook
```

### Data Management
```bash
# Check data directory
ls -la data/

# Verify PDF files are present
find data/ -name "*.pdf"
```

